# EAS uses this file instead of `.gitignore` when it builds remotely. Keep the same exclusions the
# workspace uses locally, but deliberately include `google-services.json` and
# `play-store-service-account.json` so the workflow-created files reach Expo's upload archive —
# remote EAS builds/submits upload a filtered project archive rather than reading the runner's
# filesystem directly.

# Continuous native generation — expo prebuild writes this and it must never be committed
# (docs/android-client-plan.md, "Framework and workspace").
/android
/ios

.expo/
dist/
web-build/
node_modules/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Sprint A4: the Firebase config for the FCM push backstop. Per-project and per-household, and
# its absence is a supported state — `plugins/withMedGuardAlarms.ts` wires Firebase in only when
# this file exists, so a build without it still produces a working APK with local alarms.
!google-services.json
!play-store-service-account.json
*.orig.*
.env*.local